// 26 U.S.C. §7401 — Authorization
fragment IRC_S7401 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind section;
    locator "section/7401";
    text en official """Authorization
No civil action for the collection or recovery of taxes, or of any fine, penalty, or forfeiture, shall be commenced unless the Secretary authorizes or sanctions the proceedings and the Attorney General or his delegate directs that the action be commenced.""";
    content_hash "sha256:acd505e46051b7de6d6be1c2ec17fce64242de5dfe7286f167b7d6cf15a5f3a4";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(a) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_A in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/a";
    text en official """(a) To issue orders, processes, and judgments
The district courts of the United States at the instance of the United States shall have such jurisdiction to make and issue in civil actions, writs and orders of injunction, and of ne exeat republica, orders appointing receivers, and such other orders and processes, and to render such judgments and decrees as may be necessary or appropriate for the enforcement of the internal revenue laws. The remedies hereby provided are in addition to and not exclusive of any and all other remedies of the United States in such courts or otherwise to enforce such laws.""";
    content_hash "sha256:f1b3f5e1553f71e273c7183c33d22f4280f88d1cc5cf9f8b33f4cf40fc9d508f";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(b) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_B in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/b";
    text en official """(b) To enforce summons
If any person is summoned under the internal revenue laws to appear, to testify, or to produce books, papers, or other data, the district court of the United States for the district in which such person resides or may be found shall have jurisdiction by appropriate process to compel such attendance, testimony, or production of books, papers, or other data.""";
    content_hash "sha256:893623de3b60422a17627fbad3152b50c5636b51dea0a2e6d280029ce71d4e9d";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(c) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_C in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/c";
    text en official """(c) For damages to United States officers or employees
Any officer or employee of the United States acting under authority of this title, or any person acting under or by authority of any such officer or employee, receiving any injury to his person or property in the discharge of his duty shall be entitled to maintain an action for damages therefor, in the district court of the United States, in the district wherein the party doing the injury may reside or shall be found.""";
    content_hash "sha256:cb1a8a13da0966f18313e04a6d6af8c1e890d5de9102b2f7fb113e69f89b7eb1";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(d) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_D in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/d";
    text en official """(d) Repealed. Pub. L. 92–310, title II, §230(d), June 6, 1972, 86 Stat. 209] [repealed]""";
    content_hash "sha256:59b48d05b813d6ee38ac8344570f1f810790ae8d5d213e00580f4649d8108ae5";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(e) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_E in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/e";
    text en official """(e) To quiet title
The United States district courts shall have jurisdiction of any action brought by the United States to quiet title to property if the title claimed by the United States to such property was derived from enforcement of a lien under this title.""";
    content_hash "sha256:26f39dab41704e4825fac0eb89b453a6ab8a6bc7b69d332a77530296902c0785";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7402(f) — Jurisdiction of district courts
fragment IRC_S7402_F in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7402/f";
    text en official """(f) General jurisdiction
For general jurisdiction of the district courts of the United States in civil actions involving internal revenue, see section 1340 of title 28 of the United States Code.""";
    content_hash "sha256:d9120ac567a72df8651247fd1354e64fbeb9257592fc287ff992c71fe16aabde";
}

// 26 U.S.C. §7402 — statutory note 4 (effectivedate-amendment-note)
fragment IRC_S7402_NOTE_4 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind note;
    locator "section/7402/note/4";
    text en official """Effective Date of 1966 Amendment
Amendment by Pub. L. 89–719 applicable after Nov. 2, 1966, regardless of when title or lien of United States arose or when lien or interest of another person was acquired, with certain exceptions, see section 114(a)–(c) of Pub. L. 89–719, set out as a note under section 6323 of this title.""";
    content_hash "sha256:9099f5a879193ad13d9f45e351e7c552df13ae62d8fad8e6a8897c1d8bbf9fa7";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7403(a) — Action to enforce lien or to subject property to payment of tax
fragment IRC_S7403_A in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7403/a";
    text en official """(a) Filing
In any case where there has been a refusal or neglect to pay any tax, or to discharge any liability in respect thereof, whether or not levy has been made, the Attorney General or his delegate, at the request of the Secretary, may direct a civil action to be filed in a district court of the United States to enforce the lien of the United States under this title with respect to such tax or liability or to subject any property, of whatever nature, of the delinquent, or in which he has any right, title, or interest, to the payment of such tax or liability. For purposes of the preceding sentence, any acceleration of payment under section 6166(g) shall be treated as a neglect to pay tax.""";
    content_hash "sha256:bdff141e2742add59bde641fee092c5d82b29011407fe15a56dc385645156d84";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7403(b) — Action to enforce lien or to subject property to payment of tax
fragment IRC_S7403_B in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7403/b";
    text en official """(b) Parties
All persons having liens upon or claiming any interest in the property involved in such action shall be made parties thereto.""";
    content_hash "sha256:e691147e8d802d251c502ea1031b02b1113b8a2d8f94aa77e4747e27f0229878";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7403(c) — Action to enforce lien or to subject property to payment of tax
fragment IRC_S7403_C in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7403/c";
    text en official """(c) Adjudication and decree
The court shall, after the parties have been duly notified of the action, proceed to adjudicate all matters involved therein and finally determine the merits of all claims to and liens upon the property, and, in all cases where a claim or interest of the United States therein is established, may decree a sale of such property, by the proper officer of the court, and a distribution of the proceeds of such sale according to the findings of the court in respect to the interests of the parties and of the United States. If the property is sold to satisfy a first lien held by the United States, the United States may bid at the sale such sum, not exceeding the amount of such lien with expenses of sale, as the Secretary directs.""";
    content_hash "sha256:5b3698089dfb131d176c6822b2ed6d75f8a2e466e2cdb67694c1b1499eb2e775";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7403(d) — Action to enforce lien or to subject property to payment of tax
fragment IRC_S7403_D in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7403/d";
    text en official """(d) Receivership
In any such proceeding, at the instance of the United States, the court may appoint a receiver to enforce the lien, or, upon certification by the Secretary during the pendency of such proceedings that it is in the public interest, may appoint a receiver with all the powers of a receiver in equity.""";
    content_hash "sha256:04ea9181d392599dfbaa512435fb85ade564f4892981a32ab86d48faef6ae7f6";
}

// 26 U.S.C. §7403 — statutory note 4 (effectivedate-amendment-note)
fragment IRC_S7403_NOTE_4 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind note;
    locator "section/7403/note/4";
    text en official """Effective Date of 1981 Amendment
Amendment by Pub. L. 97–34 applicable to estates of decedents dying after Dec. 31, 1981, see section 422(f)(1) of Pub. L. 97–34, set out as a note under section 6166 of this title.
Effective Date of 1966 Amendment
Amendment by Pub. L. 89–719 applicable after Nov. 2, 1966, regardless of when title or lien of United States arose or when lien or interest of another person was acquired, with certain exceptions, see section 114(a)–(c) of Pub. L. 89–719, set out as a note under section 6323 of this title.""";
    content_hash "sha256:d5ae290217fccf9a6a345a8a3aeae6d736cbfb8625fedf872b42218f8ff65d7c";
}

// 26 U.S.C. §7404 — Authority to bring civil action for estate taxes
fragment IRC_S7404 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind section;
    locator "section/7404";
    text en official """Authority to bring civil action for estate taxes
If the estate tax imposed by chapter 11 is not paid on or before the due date thereof, the Secretary shall proceed to collect the tax under the provisions of general law; or appropriate proceedings in the name of the United States may be commenced in any court of the United States having jurisdiction to subject the property of the decedent to be sold under the judgment or decree of the court. From the proceeds of such sale the amount of the tax, together with the costs and expenses of every description to be allowed by the court, shall be first paid, and the balance shall be deposited according to the order of the court, to be paid under its direction to the person entitled thereto. This section insofar as it applies to the collection of a deficiency shall be subject to the provisions of sections 6213 and 6601.""";
    content_hash "sha256:965d652838a5b113ff8172b62e6159b4a7205cf78a1d84dc28e08af72ad24c45";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7405(a) — Action for recovery of erroneous refunds
fragment IRC_S7405_A in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7405/a";
    text en official """(a) Refunds after limitation period
Any portion of a tax imposed by this title, refund of which is erroneously made, within the meaning of section 6514, may be recovered by civil action brought in the name of the United States.""";
    content_hash "sha256:8da4952b2d2df87322988ac0fa704885a07882cce729e906650bc88fde0b7715";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7405(b) — Action for recovery of erroneous refunds
fragment IRC_S7405_B in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7405/b";
    text en official """(b) Refunds otherwise erroneous
Any portion of a tax imposed by this title which has been erroneously refunded (if such refund would not be considered as erroneous under section 6514) may be recovered by civil action brought in the name of the United States.""";
    content_hash "sha256:3ffae962df8a136af28618edaf07352ab8530d1f01fcab9e117124da278295fa";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7405(c) — Action for recovery of erroneous refunds
fragment IRC_S7405_C in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7405/c";
    text en official """(c) Interest
For provision relating to interest on erroneous refunds, see section 6602.""";
    content_hash "sha256:d37037951e604a3d4dc6dc3163002303725ee3a20ac49594b696200ed3ed6b00";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7405(d) — Action for recovery of erroneous refunds
fragment IRC_S7405_D in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7405/d";
    text en official """(d) Periods of limitation
For periods of limitations on actions under this section, see section 6532(b).""";
    content_hash "sha256:b1889f155c2fdf429ad0b51f1cdb5b047955d447ee4d1445ec63570fc5046ce9";
}

// 26 U.S.C. §7406 — Disposition of judgments and moneys recovered
fragment IRC_S7406 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind section;
    locator "section/7406";
    text en official """Disposition of judgments and moneys recovered
All judgments and moneys recovered or received for taxes, costs, forfeitures, and penalties shall be paid to the Secretary as collections of internal revenue taxes.""";
    content_hash "sha256:344e49e6f0ff093fdc073a93fadbfbdcafd0394b6120cd38e4972f5c272fc573";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7407(a) — Action to enjoin tax return preparers
fragment IRC_S7407_A in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7407/a";
    text en official """(a) Authority to seek injunction
A civil action in the name of the United States to enjoin any person who is a tax return preparer from further engaging in any conduct described in subsection (b) or from further acting as a tax return preparer may be commenced at the request of the Secretary. Any action under this section shall be brought in the District Court of the United States for the district in which the tax return preparer resides or has his principal place of business or in which the taxpayer with respect to whose tax return the action is brought resides. The court may exercise its jurisdiction over such action (as provided in section 7402(a)) separate and apart from any other action brought by the United States against such tax return preparer or any taxpayer.""";
    content_hash "sha256:1b61ea4126e725d53ddd354b41eda22a0c8553ca0531841cffb197749cd83da4";
}

// 26 U.S.C. 7407(b) — Action to enjoin tax return preparers
fragment IRC_S7407_B in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind subsection;
    locator "section/7407/b";
    text en official """(b) Adjudication and decrees
In any action under subsection (a), if the court finds—
(1) that a tax return preparer has—
(A) engaged in any conduct subject to penalty under section 6694 or 6695, or subject to any criminal penalty provided by this title,
(B) misrepresented his eligibility to practice before the Internal Revenue Service, or otherwise misrepresented his experience or education as a tax return preparer,
(C) guaranteed the payment of any tax refund or the allowance of any tax credit, or
(D) engaged in any other fraudulent or deceptive conduct which substantially interferes with the proper administration of the Internal Revenue laws, and
(2) that injunctive relief is appropriate to prevent the recurrence of such conduct,
the court may enjoin such person from further engaging in such conduct. If the court finds that a tax return preparer has continually or repeatedly engaged in any conduct described in subparagraphs (A) through (D) of this subsection and that an injunction prohibiting such conduct would not be sufficient to prevent such person's interference with the proper administration of this title, the court may enjoin such person from acting as a tax return preparer.""";
    content_hash "sha256:e26e10591896354a134ef00a41c5d9473269bab31a296a3ed116b5dda8c86396";
}

// 26 U.S.C. §7407 — statutory note 5 (effectivedate-amendment-note)
fragment IRC_S7407_NOTE_5 in IRC_2024_EDITION {
    kind note;
    locator "section/7407/note/5";
    text en official """Effective Date of 2007 Amendment
Amendment by Pub. L. 110–28 applicable to returns prepared after May 25, 2007, see section 8246(c) of Pub. L. 110–28, set out as a note under section 6060 of this title.
